<Project>

  <!--
    Universal build settings for quantdale/simple-walk-game.

    Every project in the repository (three production libraries, the headless
    simulation CLI, and the three xUnit test projects) inherits this file. Each
    setting is declared EXACTLY ONCE here; the per-project files carry only what
    is genuinely project-specific (TargetFramework, OutputType, ImplicitUsings,
    IsPackable, ProjectReference, PackageReference).

    Scope rules, deliberately narrow:
      * TargetFramework is NOT set here. The three production layers must stay on
        netstandard2.1 (an architecture rule, see scripts/verify-architecture.sh)
        while the CLI and the test projects target net9.0. Each project therefore
        declares its own, which also keeps the architecture gate's grep honest.
      * LangVersion is NOT set here either. The production layers are pinned to
        C# 9.0 (see src/Directory.Build.props) because they must compile for
        netstandard2.1 with a polyfilled IsExternalInit; the net9.0 projects need
        the SDK default, which admits C# 10+ syntax the test suite already uses
        (file-scoped namespaces).

    Warnings policy: a warning is an error, everywhere, with no exclusions. It was
    explicit-false in one production csproj and implicit-false in the others before
    this file existed, so a new analyzer or compiler warning passed silently. The
    eight pre-existing xUnit analyzer warnings were fixed (assertion shape, not
    assertion meaning) rather than suppressed before the policy was switched on.
    See docs/DECISIONS.md (D-051) and openspec change
    pin-build-toolchain-and-centralize-packages.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <WarningLevel>5</WarningLevel>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>false</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
